From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: v8: ppc64 drop the DS-form alignment restriction from compressed loads

SelectLoadOpcode returns an opcode and an ImmediateMode, and VisitLoadCommon
picks the displacement form (kMode_MRI) only if CanBeImmediate(offset, mode)
accepts the offset; kInt16Imm_4ByteAligned additionally demands
!(value & 3).  Three sites downgrade to that mode for loads whose result
representation is Compressed -- AnyTagged/TaggedPointer and TaggedSigned in
the Turboshaft overload, and kCompressed in the LoadRepresentation overload
the atomic loads use -- because they emitted kPPC_LoadWordS32, i.e. lwa.
lwa is DS-form: the low two bits of its displacement are the extended
opcode, so assembler-ppc.cc CHECKs !(offset & 3) and emits LD | ... |
offset | 2.

Since ppc64le-v8-compressed-load-zero-extend.patch those sites return
kPPC_LoadWordU32, i.e. lwz, which is D-form: d_form(LWZ, ...) checks only
is_int16, and ASSEMBLE_LOAD_INTEGER(lwz, plwz, lwzx, false) passes
must_be_aligned = false, so a misaligned kMode_MRI displacement is emitted as
a plain lwz.  The downgrade no longer protects anything; that patch noted it
had become "merely unnecessary".  This removes it.

It is not a corner case.  On ppc64 the load-store simplification converts
tagged-base loads into raw loads and folds field_offset - kHeapObjectTag into
the index constant (kNeedsUntaggedBase, load-store-simplification-reducer.h).
Under pointer compression fields are 4-byte aligned and kHeapObjectTag is 1,
so every such displacement is 3 mod 4: the map is at -1, a FixedArray length
at 3.  CanBeImmediate rejects all of them, VisitLoadCommon falls through to
kMode_MRR, and the constant is materialised:

    li    r0,-1
    lwzx  rT,rB,r0

where

    lwz   rT,-1(rB)

encodes directly.  The loads concerned are those the decompression
optimization narrows to a Compressed result -- any load whose every use is
a tagged comparison, a store into a tagged field, a FrameState or a 32-bit
bitcast (decompression-optimization.cc, ProcessOperation: ComparisonOp,
WordBinopOp and ShiftOp force decompression only for Word64 reps).  A map
check is the commonest: the loaded map is compared against a constant map.
The fix is one instruction and one register fewer per such load.

Kept as they are: Int64/Word64 and uncompressed tagged loads still use ld,
which is DS-form, and keep the downgrade; VisitWord64Sar's folded lwa (~line
990) tests kInt16Imm_4ByteAligned itself and is untouched; the kInt34Imm
POWER10 path is untouched.  No new instruction is emitted -- lwz is what the
same site already emits in the MRR form -- so this is valid for both the
POWER8 (ISA 2.07) and POWER9 (ISA 3.0) pools.

Ordering: this must apply after ppc64le-v8-compressed-load-zero-extend.patch,
on whose hunks it sits.  With lwa still in place, lifting the restriction
would send a 3 mod 4 displacement into ASSEMBLE_LOAD_INTEGER's plwa branch,
whose CHECK(PPC_10_PLUS) fails on both pools.  Not separately benchmarked:
the saving is static, one instruction and the scratch register per
compressed-result load.  Upstreamable as-is together with the zero-extend
change; not ppc64le packaging specific.

--- a/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/instruction-selector-ppc.cc
+++ b/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/instruction-selector-ppc.cc
@@ -214,14 +214,12 @@
     case MemoryRepresentation::AnyTagged():
     case MemoryRepresentation::TaggedPointer():
       if (result_rep == RegisterRepresentation::Compressed()) {
-        if (*mode != kInt34Imm) *mode = kInt16Imm_4ByteAligned;
         return kPPC_LoadWordU32;
       }
       DCHECK_EQ(result_rep, RegisterRepresentation::Tagged());
       return kPPC_LoadDecompressTagged;
     case MemoryRepresentation::TaggedSigned():
       if (result_rep == RegisterRepresentation::Compressed()) {
-        if (*mode != kInt34Imm) *mode = kInt16Imm_4ByteAligned;
         return kPPC_LoadWordU32;
       }
       DCHECK_EQ(result_rep, RegisterRepresentation::Tagged());
@@ -278,7 +276,6 @@
     case MachineRepresentation::kCompressedPointer:  // Fall through.
     case MachineRepresentation::kCompressed:
 #ifdef V8_COMPRESS_POINTERS
-      if (*mode != kInt34Imm) *mode = kInt16Imm_4ByteAligned;
       return kPPC_LoadWordU32;
 #else
       UNREACHABLE();
